  select 'Egyptian Stuffed Grape Leaves (Warak Enab Mahshi)', 'In a large pot, bring water to a boil. Blanch the grape leaves by adding them to the boiling water for about 1–2 minutes. This will soften the leaves and make them more pliable. Drain and set aside.
In a mixing bowl, combine the long-grain rice, finely chopped onion, fresh parsley, fresh dill, fresh mint, olive oil, lemon juice, ground cumin, ground coriander, salt, and pepper. Mix well to ensure the ingredients are evenly distributed.
